+dimensionless target	log |M|^2 with its units removed by the event's own scales (the product of its emission scales), trained with dimensionless inputs (momenta over the collision energy) and the coupling orders as features
+context vector	16 learned numbers per training process, added to every particle's encoding and zeroed on half the training events; a held-out process is read with it at zero, or with it fitted on a few labelled events
+catalog_v3	the third process catalog (2026-10-23): MadGraph tree and one-loop amplitudes for e+e-, quark and gluon beams and two BSM models, collision energy from threshold to 1 TeV, one pool per class of processes equal up to relabelling, held-out sets H1 to H7
+catalog_v4	catalog_v3's processes regenerated with wider coverage (2026-10-25): acceptance as at a hadron collider (pT > 10 GeV, abs(eta) < 5), collision energy up to 6 TeV, a forward-angle component, every electroweak diagram, a massless b quark
+H1	held-out set, new combinations: processes whose particles, multiplicity and coupling order are all seen in training, never together (about 5% of the classes, drawn at random)
+H2	held-out set, multiplicity: the 2->4 processes of families whose 2->2 and 2->3 members train, plus 2->5 processes (a trained 2->4 with one more gluon or photon)
+H3	held-out set, particle content: every process with an external top quark (mass 172.5 GeV); the training has a top-like quark at 50, 300 and 600 GeV
+H4	held-out set, vertex: processes with four or more external W, Z or photons, at least two of them W (the quartic gauge vertex); held out only in the run trained without them
+H5	held-out set, perturbative order: one-loop amplitudes of processes whose one loop is not trained (15% of the coloured one-loop classes, and the one loop of every held-out tree)
+H6	held-out set, parameter: the strong coupling alpha_s(M_Z) = 0.13 on the families trained at 0.09 and 0.15
+H7	held-out set, energy and cuts: training processes read outside the trained region, at collision energies above it (1 to 10 TeV for catalog_v3, 6 to 20 TeV for catalog_v4) and with every final particle at pT >= 30 GeV
+zero-shot	a held-out process scored by the pretrained network with no training on it
+fine-tune	a pretrained network trained further on one process, all its weights updated
+Muon	the optimizer used since 2026-10-26: each hidden weight matrix gets an orthogonalised update (Muon), the other parameters AdamW
+AdamW	Adam with decoupled weight decay, the optimizer before Muon
+relabelled processes	held-out processes whose |M|^2 equals a training process's up to a relabelling of the particles and a constant factor
+new processes	held-out processes with no relabelling of themselves in training
+level of the error	the squared mean, over a process's events, of the error on log |M|^2: an overall offset
+shape of the error	the variance of that error over the events: what remains once the offset is removed
